<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <!--
    The lifecycle contract Valve's game systems implement, and nothing else.

    **A true leaf: no ProjectReference, deliberately.** That is what lets Audio and Scene both
    depend on it without depending on each other — Audio does not reference Scene, and inverting
    that to gain an interface would be serving a shape rather than a need (D92's test: does a
    project boundary FORBID something? this one forbids a lifecycle contract from ever coming to
    depend on a decoder, a scene or a renderer type).

    **It carries no payload for the same reason Valve's does not.** `IGameSystem::LevelInitPreEntity()`
    takes no parameters (`game/shared/igamesystem.h:39`); a system pulls what it needs from globals
    rather than being handed a level. That was checked before this project existed, because the
    assistant had claimed a shared interface was impossible on the grounds that it would need
    `LoadedMap` visible to Audio — one grep of the header killed the claim.

    net10.0 rather than net10.0-windows, like Logging and Scene: the measurement boxes are Linux and
    a contract locked to Windows would lock every implementer with it.
  -->
  <PropertyGroup>
    <TargetFramework>net10.0</TargetFramework>
    <RootNamespace>Tf2DemoSalvage.GameSystems</RootNamespace>
  </PropertyGroup>

</Project>
